# Round 18, C1-11 (follows). Two replace rows of one input known the same day, on disjoint spans: each replaces the
# earlier row on its own span (L §4.6 step 2); L §8.3's LOAD-REPLACE row no longer has "two replace lines of <x>[keys]
# known the same day". March to May read v2's 150, July and August v3's 170, the rest v1's 100.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rate: money PLN
def r[d in days]: money PLN = rate at d
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rate = 100
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace rate = 150 governs 2026-03..2026-05
version v3
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace rate = 170 governs 2026-07..2026-08
ask q: r[2026-01-15], r[2026-04-15], r[2026-06-15], r[2026-07-15]
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 150.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 170.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-12-31
